-- comment decodes, once, the HTML entities the removed input filter of lutece-core 8 (sanitizeFilterMode, LUT-34109) wrote into the plain text values: the default message of the resubmit and complete tasks and its copies shown to the user, and the response values the tasks compare with or write into the form responses (genericattributes decodes the responses: the values must follow, or the conditions no longer match). The question codes and the histories of the edited responses are left as they are.
-- This changeset rewrites the data of the site. Back up the database before the upgrade. It must run ONCE only: run
-- again, it would decode a second time a text that really holds an entity (a typed &lt; stored as &amp;lt; becomes &lt;
-- once, then < the second time). Only the values matching LIKE '%&%;%' are concerned; to list them before the upgrade,
-- run the WHERE clauses below in a SELECT.
